==Battleground==
*1 [[Dhalsim (Enemy)|Dhalsim]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Guile (Enemy)|Guile]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6 seconds<sup>180f</sup>, delay 19.33~20 seconds<sup>580f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 19.33~20 seconds<sup>580f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 99.33~100 seconds<sup>2,980f~3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 99.33 seconds<sup>2,980f</sup>, delay 99.33~100 seconds<sup>2,980f~3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 99.33~100 seconds<sup>2,980f~3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The peons in this stage will always come in groups, so it's easy to tell when they'll spawn. Area attack units like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] can quickly get rid of them and also chip damage off of the boss. Dhalsim and Guile have low DPS so tankers like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] are good damage dealers and can also handle the hits. Ranged units also work wonders here.

